softhsm
------------------------------------------
SoftHSM is an implementation of a cryptographic store accessible through a
PKCS#11 interface.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.11-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libsqlite3_0-3.49.1-1
  libssl3-3.5.9-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20260320-2
  binutils-2.47-1
  cppunit-1.13.2-1
  cygport-0.37.11-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libp11-kit-devel-0.26.5-1
  libsqlite3-devel-3.49.1-1
  libssl-devel-3.5.9-1
  libtool-2.6.2-1
  make-4.4.1-2
  sqlite3-3.49.1-1

Canonical website:
  https://www.softhsm.org/

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/softhsm/SoftHSMv2/archive/refs/tags/2.7.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack softhsm-2.7.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./softhsm-2.7.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/softhsm-2.7.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/softhsm-2.7.0-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(softhsm)
  /etc/softhsm2.conf
  /etc/softhsm2.conf.sample
  /usr/bin/softhsm2-dump-file.exe
  /usr/bin/softhsm2-keyconv.exe
